      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-330958",
      ":question/problem": "$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{\u2032}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+3 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{\u2032}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L{{x}_{1}(t)}=\\frac{1}{s-1}-\\frac{3}{s},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L{{x}_{2}(t)}=\\frac{1/2}{s-1}-\\frac{1}{s}+\\frac{3/2}{s-3}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |"
